  "solution": {
    "text": "As anion is same, the covalent character in ionic compound will depend upon the size and charge on the cation. According to fajan's rule,<br />Covalent nature ∝ charge on cation<br /><math> <mrow>  <mtext>PbO</mtext></mrow></math> is most ionic as it has <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow></msub></math> is most covalent as it has <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup></math> ."
